cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite the versioned release below. Zenodo assigns its version DOI when the GitHub release is published; consult that release for the archive DOI."
version: 4.1.0
title: "The I3322 quantum value is attained spatially but not in finite dimension"
type: article
authors:
  - given-names: Seth
    family-names: Douglas
    email: apsiape@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4708-3252"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Apsiape/i3322-exact-wall"
url: "https://github.com/Apsiape/i3322-exact-wall/releases/tag/v4.1.0"
abstract: >-
  The tensor-product and commuting-operator suprema of the canonical I3322
  Bell functional coincide at a common value S, certified within an exact
  two-sided window of width 3.61e-9 (the exact value beyond the window
  remains open). A spatial strategy on l2(Z) tensor l2(Z) attains S, while no
  finite-dimensional strategy does - proving the 2010 conjecture of Pal and
  Vertesi. Consequently C_q(3,3;2,2) is not closed and differs from
  C_qs(3,3;2,2), at the smallest venue by input count, among two-outcome
  bipartite scenarios, in which nonclosure is known; no minimality is claimed
  over scenarios with larger output alphabets. The paper further proves the
  dimension complexity D(eps) = Theta(log(1/eps)), with explicit derived
  upper bound D(eps) <= 23.9010650 log(1/eps) for all sufficiently small
  eps. The lower proof is a finite weighted-flow argument with existential
  constants. Lean checks cover 37 selected declarations; the complete
  analytic proof is not formalized. Concurrent work is credited to
  Pauwels (arXiv:2608.29734v1) and Coladangelo (arXiv:2609.06038v1).
keywords:
  - Bell inequalities
  - I3322
  - quantum correlations
  - commuting operators
  - computer-assisted proof
  - nonattainment
  - quantum spatial correlations
  - Cq versus Cqs
  - nonclosed quantum correlations
  - minimal Bell scenario
